 "metadata": {
  "soundFile": "/Volumes/External/DevExteralHD/1. Current /MindAR with example/assets/HappyBirthday.vocals.wav",
  "duration": 30.55,
  "manualEdits": [
   "The sung chorus and 'on the day you came to be' were rebuilt from word-aligned lyrics: consonants stay brief while vowels hold for the sung note.",
   "All four sung 'to ya' phrases use B/E/C/D: brief T/S mouth, held Oo, Y/Eh transition, then Ah. Re-running Rhubarb discards these edits; raw capture kept as HappyBirthday.vocals.rhubarb.raw.json"
  ],
  "handEdits": [
   "11.25-11.82 B split into B+A so the phrase end of 'party' closes the lips instead of holding a stretch",
   "Each chorus 'b' of Birthday is now A (0.12s lips closed) then F (puckered release) \u2014 a bilabial plosive is a closure followed by a rounded release, not a single shape.",
   "The 'to' of each sung 'to ya' changed E->F: /tu:/ is a UW, which is Rhubarb's full pucker, not its slight round",
   "1.16-1.25 B silenced to X: the vocal stem has an isolated 0.08s breath there, not a word",
   "The '-py' of each 'happy' changed H->B: it is an EE, which Rhubarb assigns to B (slightly open, clenched teeth). H was leaving the jaw wide open between the two lip closures either side."
  ]
 },
